course: dictionary
lesson: 9845
title: Swollen, bigger than normal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Swollen means bigger than normal. You often see it when a part of the body is hurt, stung or ill. «A sore, red, swollen toe beside the nail may be an ingrown toenail, so you tell a parent.» The words sore and red are clues that something is wrong, and swollen tells you the toe has grown bigger than it should be.
explain: Swollen is the past form of the verb swell, which means to grow bigger. Swell, swells, swelled, swollen: you can say «The river has swollen» or «The river has swelled». Both mean it has grown bigger, so you can use swollen as a describing word too, as in «a swollen river».
explain: Look at the words around swollen to check its meaning. «A swollen river» comes after heavy rain, and the dictionary says it has more water than usual. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The river has more water than usual» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Swollen means bigger than normal.
fact: Swollen can describe a body part, as in «a swollen ankle» or «swollen glands».
fact: A swollen river has more water than usual after rain, and it can flood.
fact: A swollen ankle may be a sprain; ice and rest help, but an adult should check it.
fact: Swell is the verb, and swollen is its past form.
exercise: «A sore, red, swollen toe beside the nail may be an ingrown toenail.» What does swollen mean here? | Painted bright red | *Bigger than normal | Smaller than normal | Cold and numb
exercise: After heavy rain, Ravi says the river is swollen. What does he mean? | *It has more water than usual | It runs uphill | It is frozen solid | It has no water at all
exercise: You fall and your ankle becomes swollen. What should you do? | Walk on it until it feels better | Run on it to make it strong | Wrap it tight and ignore it | *Use ice and rest, and let an adult check it
test: «A carrot is a swollen root that stores food.» What does swollen mean in this sentence? | *Bigger than normal, because it stores food | Dried out | Thin and straight | Cold and hard
test: Which word is closest in meaning to swollen? | *Enlarged | Shrunken | Thin | Frozen
exam: Mia says swollen means smaller than normal. Is she right? | Yes, it means cold and stiff | Yes, it means smaller than normal | No, it means exactly normal | *No, swollen means bigger than normal
